cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Depth-harmonised soil organic carbon mapping for Madagascar"
abstract: >-
  Python code to map soil organic carbon stocks in Madagascar for 0-30, 30-100 and
  0-100 cm. Profiles sampled only to 30 cm are completed with the Jobbagy and
  Jackson (2000) exponential depth model calibrated on profiles measured to 1 m.
  Random Forest, XGBoost and quantile regression forest models are tuned and
  evaluated with random and spatial block nested cross-validation, interpreted
  with SHAP and partial dependence, and used to produce national maps with
  bootstrap uncertainty and QRF prediction-interval rasters.
